    "trust_rule_corrections_made_during_collection": [
      "La Habra's PV Toolkit PDF was initially summarized by the fetch tool with several details that turned out not to appear in the actual document text once directly read via the saved-file Read technique (a fabricated 'proof of property ownership' requirement, an unsupported '2025 version' claim). The record was built from the directly-read PDF content only, discarding the inaccurate initial summary — a concrete instance of why this session's established practice of re-reading saved PDFs directly, rather than trusting a fetch tool's first-pass summary, matters.",
      "Seal Beach's real fee figures ($0 plan-check/permit fee, $51 inspection fee) came from a directly-read official PDF, not search synthesis — Seal Beach is also notable for requiring Planning Division review for all solar PV installations regardless of size, a deviation from the more common 'no planning review at this size' pattern seen in most other cities this campaign."
    ]
